<DetailLayout 
  title="QC Gate" 
  heading="Quality Control Pipeline"
  description="Deterministic testing and verification for the data_rein harness."
>
  <p>Every commit, PR, and agent execution path is validated against the deterministic Quality Control (QC) pipeline.</p>

  <h2>Verification Suite</h2>
  <p>The standard verification suite checks functionality, style, and architectural compliance across the entire working tree.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>pytest Suite:</strong> 400 unit, integration, and contract tests strictly verified via GitHub Actions and local pre-push gates.</li>
    <li><strong>PON Tester:</strong> Validates `os.system` boundaries, circuit breaker implementations, and zero-polling limits.</li>
    <li><strong>Type & Lint:</strong> Zero-tolerance policy on Ruff and basedpyright (0 errors, 0 warnings).</li>
    <li><strong>Security Scans:</strong> Bandit and `pip-audit` to guarantee no known vulnerabilities.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Automated Quality Control</h2>
  <p>Any failure in the QC pipeline blocks execution and logs a failover task to the Universal Task Trail. Agents cannot circumvent these checks when submitting pull requests or modifying the shared knowledge base.</p>
</DetailLayout>
